{"availability":"available","full":"lsegal/zvidlib","name":"zvidlib","description":"A library for video","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-20T03:58:14Z","updated":"2026-10-09T18:04:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lsegal.github.io/zvidlib/","topics":[],"demo":"https://lsegal.github.io/zvidlib/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.838Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.838Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.838Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:40:01.365Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:02.838Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Frame-exact video and sample-exact audio for Rust and the browser.","Website and live demo · API docs · crates.io · docs.rs · Releases","zvidlib decodes, encodes and muxes video and audio: HEVC, AV1, VP8 and VP9 video and AAC, Opus and Vorbis audio, in MP4 and WebM. It runs natively and in WebAssembly from one API. Ask for frame n with get(n) and you get exactly frame n, even in streams full of B-frames and long groups of pictures. Ask for a sample range and you get exactly those samples. Write frame n with put(n) and zvidlib encodes it, keeps the audio aligned to it, and muxes the result into a file any player can open."],"features":["Frame-exact indexed get and put. Every read returns the frame you asked for, never the nearest keyframe. zvidlib keeps decoded frames and decoder state between requests, so sequential access stays fast. A seek-preview…","Sample-exact audio. AAC, Opus and Vorbis decode and encode alongside the video. Read any exact sample range (AudioSampleReader natively, AudioStream.getRange() in the browser), or exactly the samples covered by a video…","One API, native and WebAssembly. The same concepts work in Rust on Windows, macOS and Linux, and in JavaScript through a wasm-bindgen package with BigInt-safe frame indices, Blob and stream I/O, and stable error codes.","Hardware first, pure Rust always. zvidlib uses NVDEC, Media Foundation (NVENC, Quick Sync, AMF), VideoToolbox and browser WebCodecs when they're available. When they aren't, it falls back to its own pure-Rust codecs,…","No FFmpeg dependency. No C toolchain, no system codec packages, no GPL. Codecs and containers are Rust crates you can trim down to what your app uses with Cargo features."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lsegal/zvidlib/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8594210da952241c6aa8f4613fe18b15c60a4233f5ea85a27795b5a68053f1fa","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T06:40:01.461Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:40:01.461Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Frame-exact video and sample-exact audio for Rust and the browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lsegal/zvidlib/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"8594210da952241c6aa8f4613fe18b15c60a4233f5ea85a27795b5a68053f1fa","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lsegal/zvidlib/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T06:40:01.461Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T06:36:33Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lsegal/zvidlib/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T06:40:01.463Z","hash":"8594210da952241c6aa8f4613fe18b15c60a4233f5ea85a27795b5a68053f1fa","originalBytes":29398,"storedBytes":29398,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["zvidlib","video","vp9","rust","frame","browser","hardware","native","av1","codec","let","web","webcodecs","cargo","pure","audio","every","media","features","hevc","release","examples","mp4","windows","back","encode","encoder","limits","new","package","target","decode","decoder","sample","api","block","crates","foundation","macos","aac","await","codecs","main","site","test","vp8","webm","build","falling","install","one","opus","track","wasm-pack","bit","canvas","factory","file","github","init","linux","nvdec","pkg","platform","read","videotoolbox","console","containers"